## 4. Pro-Tip: Preloading Strategies

Lazy loading makes the initial load fast, but the user might see a "flicker" or delay when clicking a lazy link for the first time.

* **`PreloadAllModules`:** This tells Angular to download the lazy chunks in the background *after* the initial app has loaded. It gives you the best of both worlds: fast initial start and instant navigation later.

> **Note:** Always ensure your lazy-loaded paths do not have "hard" imports in the `app.component.ts` or `app.module.ts`, otherwise, they will be bundled into the main file, defeating the purpose of lazy loading!
